- at temp pointer t, `neg = (*t=='-')`, q=t+neg;
- bounds-safe memcpy/load uint32 from q (valid format guarantees q has 3 or 4 temp chars plus newline, so 4 bytes available even at EOF);
- `two = q[1] != '.'` determined from word bytes;
- compute both one-digit and two-digit integer-tenths values from packed bytes, select without branch if compiler permits, apply sign branchlessly;
- set p directly to q + 4 + two (after newline).
